hadiths[36]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16774","Abd Allah said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, and he is al-Muqaddami, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, that he gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) game meat, and he did not accept it; he saw that in the face of al-Sab and said: Nothing prevented us from accepting from you except that we were in ihram."
"16775","He said: And he was asked about horses trampling the children of polytheists at night; he said: They, meaning, are of their fathers."
"16776","And he said: There is no hima except for Allah and for His Messenger."
"16777","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to me, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was at al-Abwa or at Waddan, and I gifted him wild ass meat while he was in ihram, and he returned it to me; when he saw dislike in my face he said: We do not return upon you, but we are in ihram."
"16778","He said: And I heard him say: There is no hima except for Allah and for His Messenger."
"16779","He said: And he was asked about the households of polytheists attacked by night, and their women and offspring are struck; he said: They are of them."
"16780","Abd Allah said: Musab, he is al-Zubayri, narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Ayyash al-Makhzumi, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama al-Laythi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made al-Naqi a hima and said: There is no hima except for Allah and for His Messenger."
"16781","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama al-Laythi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild ass while he was at al-Abwa or at Waddan, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what was in my face he said: We returned it upon you only because we are in ihram."
"16782","Abd Allah said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways Abd Allah ibn Uways narrated to us, I heard from him during the caliphate of al-Mahdi, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, he said: I gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hamstrung wild ass at Waddan, or he said: at al-Abwa; he said: So he returned it to me; when he saw the severity of that in my face he said: We only returned it to you because we are in ihram."
"16783","He said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Salih ibn Kaysan narrate, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at Waddan, al-Sab ibn Jaththama or a man came to him with part of a wild ass, and he returned it upon him and said: We are in ihram, we do not eat game."
"16784","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no hima except for Allah and His Messenger."
"16785","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, our horses trampled the children of the polytheists; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are of their fathers."
"16786","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, he said: Hammad narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, he said: He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Waddan with a wild ass, and he returned it upon him and said: We are in ihram, we do not eat game."
"16787","Amir ibn Salih al-Zubayri narrated to us in the year one hundred eighty, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no hima except for Allah and for His Messenger."
"16788","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Humayd al-Himsi Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira ibn Sayyar narrated to me, he said: Haywa narrated to us, he said: Baqiyya narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Rashid ibn Sad, he said: When Istakhr was conquered, a caller called: Indeed the Dajjal has come out; he said: al-Sab ibn Jaththama met them and said: Were it not for what you say, I would inform you that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal does not come out until people are heedless of mentioning him and until the imams leave mentioning him on the minbars."
"16789","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Abu Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama al-Laythi, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the house of the houses of the polytheists we assault by night, how about who is under the raid of children; he said: They are of them."
"16790","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj of the people of Marw in the year two hundred twenty-eight informed us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, al-Sab ibn Jaththama informed him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the households of the polytheists attacked by night, and their women and offspring are struck; he said: They are of them."
"16791","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we strike in the night attack from the offspring of the polytheists; he said: They are of them."
"16792","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to me, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, informed us, he said: my father informed us, from Salih, meaning Ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed him that Ibn Abbas informed him that al-Sab ibn Jaththama informed him that he gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild ass while he was at Waddan, and he returned it upon him; he said: When he saw what was in my face he said: We returned it upon you only because we are in ihram."
"16793","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Ibn akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud informed me that Abd Allah ibn Abbas used to say: I heard al-Sab ibn Jaththama ibn Qays al-Laythi say: I gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild ass at al-Abwa, and he returned it upon me; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recognized in my face dislike of his returning, he said: It is not our returning upon you, but we are in ihram."
"16794","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi informed us, he said: Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud informed me that Abd Allah ibn Abbas informed him that he heard al-Sab ibn Jaththama al-Laythi, and he was from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), inform that he gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild ass at al-Abwa or at Waddan, while the Prophet was in ihram, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it; al-Sab said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recognized in my face his returning my gift, he said: It is not our returning upon you, but I am in ihram."
"16795","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Habib Luwayn narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came until when he was at Waddan, a Bedouin gifted him game meat, and he returned it and said: We do not eat game."
"16796","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a wild ass, and he returned it upon him and said: We are in ihram, we do not eat game."
"16797","Abd Allah narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Masud, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, we assault the house or houses of the polytheists at night, with them their boys and women, and we kill them; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are of them."
"16798","He said: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-Zanji, he said: I saw al-Zuhri dyeing his head with black."
"16799","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shumayl, meaning al-Nadr, informed us, he said: Muhammad, he is Ibn Amr, informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Sab ibn Jaththama al-Laythi, he said: He used to narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hadiths; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no hima except for Allah and for His Messenger."
"16800","He said: And I gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild ass while he was in ihram, and he returned it upon me; he recognized that in my face and said: We returned it upon you only because we are in ihram."
"16801","And I asked him about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Kill them along with them. He said: And he had forbidden it concerning them on the day of Khaybar."
"16802","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, meaning al-Humaydi, narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama al-Laythi informed me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was asked about the households of the polytheists who are attacked at night and some of their women and offspring are hit, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are from them."
"16803","And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no protected pasture except for Allah and for His Messenger."
"16804","And I gave as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the meat of a wild ass while he was at al-Abwa or at Waddan, and he returned it to me, and when he saw displeasure in my face he said: It is not a rejection of you on our part, but we are in a state of ihram."
"16805","Sufyan said: And Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us this hadith of al-Sa'b from al-Zuhri before we met him, and he said in it: They are from their fathers, and when al-Zuhri came to us I checked it with him and he did not say it, and he said: They are better than them."
"16806","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Amr Abu Sulayman al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba from Ibn Abbas that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a dwelling of the dwellings of the polytheists which we attack at dawn for a raid, and we strike the children beneath the bellies of the horses without realizing, and he said: They are from them."
"16807","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Maslama informed us from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba ibn Mas'ud from Abd Allah ibn Abbas from al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama al-Laythi that he gave as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at al-Abwa or at Waddan, a wild ass, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it to him, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what was in his face he said: We did not return it to you except that we are in a state of ihram."
"16808","Abd Allah narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada informed us with the like of it, meaning from Malik, and Rawh said: his face."
"16809","He said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym informed us, he said: Ibn Uyayna narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah from Ibn Abbas from al-Sa'b ibn Jaththama, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no protected pasture except for Allah and His Messenger."
